#: mouse.cpp:90
msgid "&General"
msgstr "&Chung"

#: mouse.cpp:95
msgid ""
"If you are left-handed, you may prefer to swap the functions of the left and "
"right buttons on your pointing device by choosing the 'left-handed' option. "
"If your pointing device has more than two buttons, only those that function "
"as the left and right buttons are affected. For example, if you have a three-"
"button mouse, the middle button is unaffected."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n thua^.n tay tra'i, ba.n co' the^? se~ thi'ch ddo^?i ca'c chu+'c"
"na(ng o+? be^n tra'i qua pha?i . (fix me!)"

#: mouse.cpp:105
msgid ""
"The default behavior in KDE is to select and activate icons with a single "
"click of the left button on your pointing device. This behavior is "
"consistent with what you would expect when you click links in most web "
"browsers. If you would prefer to select with a single click, and activate "
"with a double click, check this option."
msgstr ""
"Cu+ xu+? ma(.c ddi.nh cu?a KDE la` cho.n ca'c icon kho^ng hoa.t ddo^.ng ba('ng"
"mo^.t cu' nha^'p chuo^.t tra'i tre^n thie^'t bi. ba.n ddang tro? to+'i . Cu+ xu+? na`y"
"cu~ng gio^'ng nhu+ khi ba.n click va`o mo^.t lie^n ke^'t trong mo^.t trang web ."
"Ne^'u ba.n muo^'n cho.n ba(`ng 1 click, ki'ch hoa.t ba(`ng 2 click, nha^.n tuy` cho.n"
"na`y ."

#: mouse.cpp:113
msgid ""
"Activates and opens a file or folder with a single click.When this option is "
"checked, the shape of the mouse pointer changes whenever it is over an icon."
msgstr ""
"Ki'ch hoa.t va` mo+? file hay thu+ mu.c vo+'i 1 click . Khi tuy` cho.n na`y ddu+o+.c"
"nha^.n, hi`nh da.ng cu?a con tro? thay ddo^?i khi no' o+? tre^n icon ."

#: mouse.cpp:121
msgid ""
"If you check this option, pausing the mouse pointer over an icon on the "
"screen will automatically select that icon. This may be useful when single "
"clicks activate icons, and you want only to select the icon without "
"activating it."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n nha^.n tuy` cho.n na`y, ta.m du+`ng con tro? tre^n icon se~ tu+. ddo^.ng"
"cho.n icon . No' co' the^? se~ hu+~u du.ng khi ba.n du`ng 1 click dde^? ki'ch hoa.t"
"icon, va` ba.n muo^'n cho.n icon va` kho^ng ki'ch hoa.t chu'ng ."

#: mouse.cpp:133
msgid ""
"If you have checked the option to automatically select icons, this slider "
"allows you to select how long the mouse pointer must be paused over the icon "
"before it is selected."
msgstr ""
"Ne^`u tuy` cho.n na`y ddu+o+.c nha^.n, icon se~ ddu+o+.c cho.n tu+. ddo^.ng,"
"thanh tru+o+.t na`y na`y cho phe'p ba.n cho.n cho icon se~ bi. ki'ch hoa.t ne^'u chuo^t"
"bi. du+`ng tre^n icon trong bao la^u ."

#: mouse.cpp:138
msgid "Show feedback when clicking an icon"
msgstr "Hie^?n thi. tho^ng tin pha?n ho^`i khi nha^'n icon"

#: mouse.cpp:143
msgid "Use high-visibility large cursor"
msgstr "Du`ng con tro? cu+.c lo+'n"

#: mouse.cpp:160
msgid "&Advanced"
msgstr "&Cao ca^'p"

#: mouse.cpp:166
msgid "Pointer Acceleration:"
msgstr "Ta(ng to^'c con tro?"

#: mouse.cpp:173
msgid ""
"This option allows you to change the relationship between the distance that "
"the mouse pointer moves on the screen and the relative movement of the "
"physical device itself (which may be a mouse, trackball, or some other "
"pointing device.)<p> A high value for the acceleration will lead to large "
"movements of the mouse pointer on the screen even when you only make a small "
"movement with the physical device. Selecting very high values may result in "
"the mouse pointer flying across the screen, making it hard to control!<p> "
"You can set the acceleration value by dragging the slider button or by "
"clicking the up/down arrows on the spin-button to the left of the slider."
msgstr ""
"This option allows you to change the relationship between the distance that "
"the mouse pointer moves on the screen and the relative movement of the "
"physical device itself (which may be a mouse, trackball, or some other "
"pointing device.)<p> A high value for the acceleration will lead to large "
"movements of the mouse pointer on the screen even when you only make a small "
"movement with the physical device. Selecting very high values may result in "
"the mouse pointer flying across the screen, making it hard to control!<p> "
"You can set the acceleration value by dragging the slider button or by "
"clicking the up/down arrows on the spin-button to the left of the slider."

#: mouse.cpp:189
msgid "Pointer Threshold:"
msgstr "Ngu+o+~ng con tro?:"

#: mouse.cpp:191 mouse.cpp:246
msgid " pixels"
msgstr " pixels"

#: mouse.cpp:196
msgid ""
"The threshold is the smallest distance that the mouse pointer must move on "
"the screen before acceleration has any effect. If the movement is smaller "
"than the threshold, the mouse pointer moves as if the acceleration was set "
"to 1X.<p> Thus, when you make small movements with the physical device, "
"there is no acceleration at all, giving you a greater degree of control over "
"the mouse pointer. With larger movements of the physical device, you can "
"move the mouse pointer rapidly to different areas on the screen.<p> You can "
"set the threshold value by dragging the slider button or by clicking the up/"
"down arrows on the spin-button to the left of the slider."
msgstr ""
"The threshold is the smallest distance that the mouse pointer must move on "
"the screen before acceleration has any effect. If the movement is smaller "
"than the threshold, the mouse pointer moves as if the acceleration was set "
"to 1X.<p> Thus, when you make small movements with the physical device, "
"there is no acceleration at all, giving you a greater degree of control over "
"the mouse pointer. With larger movements of the physical device, you can "
"move the mouse pointer rapidly to different areas on the screen.<p> You can "
"set the threshold value by dragging the slider button or by clicking the up/"
"down arrows on the spin-button to the left of the slider."

#: mouse.cpp:213
msgid "Double Click Interval:"
msgstr "Khoa?ng tho+`i gian click ke'p:"

#: mouse.cpp:215 mouse.cpp:233
msgid " ms"
msgstr " ms"

#: mouse.cpp:220
msgid ""
"The double click interval is the maximal time (in milliseconds) between two "
"mouse clicks which turns them into a double click. If the second click "
"happens later than this time interval after the first click, they are "
"recognized as two separate clicks."
msgstr ""
"Khoa?ng tho+`i gian click ke'p la` khoa?ng tho+`i lo+'n nha^'t (ms) giu+~a 2 la^`n"
"nha^'n chuo^.t  ddee^? la`m cho cho chu'ng tro+? tha`nh click ke'p ."
"Ne^'u la^`n click thu+' 2 xa?y ra muo^.n ho+n khoa?ng tho+`i gian na`y, no' se~"
"ddu+o+.c coi la` 2 la^`n click ddo+n ."

#: mouse.cpp:231
msgid "Drag Start Time:"
msgstr "Tho+`i gian ba('t dda^`u ke'o( drag):"

#: mouse.cpp:238
msgid ""
"If you click with the mouse (e.g. in a multi-line editor) and begin to move "
"the mouse within the drag start time, a drag operation will be initiated."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n click vo+'i chuo^.t ( vi' du. trong tri`nh soa.n tha?o multi-line) va` ba('t"
"dda^`u di chuye^?n chuo^.t trong khoa?ng tho+`i gian ba('t dda^u, thao ta'c tha? (drag)"
"se~ ddu+o+.c kho+?i ta.o . "

#: mouse.cpp:244
msgid "Drag Start Distance:"
msgstr "Khoa?ng ca'ch ba('t dda^`u tha? ( drag)"

#: mouse.cpp:251
msgid ""
"If you click with the mouse and begin to move the mouse at least the drag "
"start distance, a drag operation will be initiated."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n click vo+'i chuo^.t va` ba('t dda^`u di chuye^?n no' vo+'i khoa?ng ca'ch"
"to^'i thie^?u la` tha?, thao ta'c tha? ( drag) se~ ddu+o+.c kho+?i ta.o ."

#: mouse.cpp:257
msgid "Mouse Wheel Scrolls By:"
msgstr "Chuo^.t ba'nh xe cuo^'n bo+?i :"

#: mouse.cpp:259
msgid " lines"
msgstr "do`ng"

#: mouse.cpp:264
msgid ""
"If you use the wheel of a mouse, this value determines the number of lines "
"to scroll for each wheel movement. Note that if this number exceeds the "
"number of visible lines, it will be ignored and the wheel movement will be "
"handled as a page up/down movement."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n la(n chuo^.t, gia' tri. na`y se~ xa'c ddi.nh so^' ca'c do`ng se~ cuo^.n trong "
"mo^'i chuye^?n ddo^.ng cuo^'n . Chu' y' la` ne^'u gia' tri. na`y vu+o+.t qua' khoa?ng"
"xem ddu+o+.c cu?a trang, no' se~ bi. bo? qua va` su+. di chuye^?n chuo^.t se~ "
"ddu+o+.c ti'nh nhu+ la` di chuye^?n thay trang ."

#: mouse.cpp:377
msgid "KDE must be restarted for the cursor size change to take effect"
msgstr ""
"KDE pha?i kho+?i ddo^.ng la.i dde^? cho su+. thay ddo^?i"
"ki'ch thu+o+'c con tro? co' ta'c du.ng ."

#: mouse.cpp:401
msgid ""
"<h1>Mouse</h1> This module allows you to choose various options for the way "
"in which your pointing device works. Your pointing device may be a mouse, "
"trackball, or some other hardware that performs a similar function."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Chuo^.t </h1> Module na`y cho phe'p ba.n cho.n nhie^`u tuy` cho.n kha'c nhau"
"theo ca'ch ma` ba.n muo^'n ca'c thie^'t bi. chuo^.t hoa.t ddo^.ng ra sao . "
"Thie^'t bi. chuo^.t co' the^? la` con chuo^.t, trackball, hay nhie^`u pha^`n cu+'ng"
"co' chu+'c na(ng tu+o+ng tu+. ."

